\documentclass[a4paper]{article}
\usepackage{fontspec}
\setmainfont{Latin Modern Roman}
\usepackage[left=22mm,right=22mm,top=22mm,bottom=22mm]{geometry}
\pagestyle{empty}
\begin{document}
The paragraph breaking algorithm considers the complete sequence of words before choosing its line endings. Typography is a system of interdependent decisions, including hyphenation, flexible spaces, and the relationship between consecutive lines. A local decision which fills the current line can create an unnecessarily loose following line. Mathematical documents require consistent composition across different widths, without inserting explicit newlines into the original source.
\end{document}

